// Title: #[tail_recursive] names causes that do not apply when an Io call or a raise does not follow the formals
// Command: timeout -s KILL 30 graphix --no-cache tests-lang-rest-a-tail-recursive-io-diagnostic.gx
// Expected: a refusal that says the body's println (an Io call that does not follow the
//   formals) keeps each depth its own activation.
// Observed: "#[tail_recursive]: every recursive call is in tail position, but no loop is
//   built — ... so with a labeled, variadic or opaque formal, or a body holding per-call
//   memory (a collection operation, or a callee holding one), every call keeps its own
//   activation" -- none of which this body has. Replacing the println with
//   `error(`E)?;` under an enclosing catch gives the same message (the handler-ful raise
//   does not follow the formals, lowering::claims_no_site_memory).
#[tail_recursive]
let rec f = |n: i64, acc: i64| -> i64 {
  println("step");
  select n { 0 => acc, _ => f(n - 1, acc + n) }
};
f(3, 0)
